Develop a retiming circuit that introduces a specified delay of two clock cycles to a parallel input of width 'n'. The module utilizes a shift register to sequentially store the input signals and output the value from the end of the delay chain, effectively allowing the designer to manage signal timing in digital systems. This design can be particularly useful for synchronizing signals in high-speed applications where timing adjustments are critical.
