description:
Design a 4-bit wide priority encoder that takes a 16-bit input, enabling the selection of the highest 4-bit segment of the input when the enable (EN) signal is active (high). The output (O) represents the index of the highest active bit in the segmented input based on the priority of groups. Note that the assigned value of temp captures the priority in a manner that allows the most significant group to dictate the output.
module top_module(
    input [15:0] I,
    input EN,
    output reg [3:0] O
);

code:
module top_module(
    input [15:0] I,
    input EN,
    output reg [3:0] O
);reg [3:0] temp;

always @ (posedge EN) begin
    temp <= I[15:12] > I[11:8] > I[7:4] > I[3:0];
end

assign O = temp[3:0];

endmodule

