Create a combinational circuit that computes the factorial of the input value \( n \) for integers ranging from 0 to 12. The output \( fact \) will provide the precomputed factorial value corresponding to the input \( n \). For inputs outside this range, the output will default to zero. This design effectively acts as a small lookup table for factorial values.
