description:
Implement the Verilog module based on the following description.
Given the finite state machine circuit described below.

// Build this circuit in Verilog.

// Input c goes to three different two-input gates: a NAND, an OR, and an XOR gate. Each of the three gates is connected to the input of a D flip-flop and then the flip-flop outputs all go to a three-input OR, whose output is W. The second input of the NAND is its corresponding flip-flop's output, the second input of the OR is its corresponding flip-flop's complemented output, and finally the second input of the XOR is its corresponding flip-flop's complementary output.
module fsm_module3 (
	input clk,
	input c,
	output w);

code:
module fsm_module3 (
	input clk,
	input c,
	output w);reg [2:0] state = 0;

	always @(posedge clk) begin
		state <= { ~(state[2] & c), state[1] | ~c, state[0] ^ ~c };
	end

	assign w = |state;

endmodule

