description:
Design a VGA buffer for storing and outputting pixel data. The module stores a 15-bit wide input value `d` into an internal memory register `mem` after a specified delay of 8192 clock cycles, driven by the `clk` input. Once the data is stored, on each positive edge of the `pixel_clk`, the stored output `q` is updated with the contents of `mem`, allowing for synchronized data output for video display purposes. This design helps facilitate the timing required for video pixel data management in VGA applications.
module top_module(
    output reg [14:0] q,
    input [14:0] d,
    input clk, pixel_clk
);

code:
module top_module(
    output reg [14:0] q,
    input [14:0] d,
    input clk, pixel_clk
);reg [14:0] mem = 0;
    reg [15:0] delay = 16'd0;

    always @ (posedge clk) begin
        if (delay == 16'd8192) begin
            mem <= d;
        end else begin
            delay <= delay + 16'b1;
        end
    end


    always @ (posedge pixel_clk) begin
        q <= mem;
    end

endmodule

